# pipeline_output holds derived products -- rebinned spectra, staged exposures,
# fit figures and their JSON records -- which are regenerated from the archive
# by the scripts in finalrun/ and are far too large to version.  Everything here
# is ignored EXCEPT the hand-authored override tables under final/, which are
# inputs rather than outputs: without them the pipeline runs and quietly
# produces different spectra.
#
# decisions.csv is NOT among them any more.  The ledger's canonical copy is
# Data/decisions.csv; a second copy lived here and went stale twice, sitting at
# 204 rows for three weeks while the real ledger passed 450.  rebin_path.py now
# names the one ledger and every reader imports it, so a copy here would be a
# duplicate with nothing reading it.  Past versions remain in git history.
*
!.gitignore
!final/
final/*
!final/spectrum_overrides.csv
!final/name_overrides.csv
# bal_status.csv is hand-curated too: which adopted objects are BALs, with
# the evidence for each.  Needed to read the Mg II sweep, where a BAL is
# EXPECTED to show the model exceeding the observed line (index 422), so a
# high ratio is a signature rather than a failure.  Text-matching the ledger
# for "BAL" does not reproduce it -- five hits are boilerplate about an
# unreliable test and three are cross-references to other objects.
!final/bal_status.csv

# EXCEPTIONS ADDED 2026-11-07, so that work which cannot be recreated in under a
# day is not held only on one disk.  GTR: "let's just make sure that we don't
# lose any work that can't be recreated in <1 day."
#
# work_queue.csv is the order -> object mapping that every folder prefix, every
# index in Table 1 and every ledger row key on.  build_work_queue.py regenerates
# it, but a rerun that produced even a slightly different ordering would shift
# every index in the paper, so in practice it is an input and not an output.
!work_queue.csv
#
# The fit RECORDS, 8.6 MB of JSON, are kept while the figures beside them (755
# MB of PNG) are not.  Each record carries the override that produced the fit,
# and FORTY-NINE ADOPTED FITS HAVE AN OVERRIDE THAT EXISTS NOWHERE ELSE -- 45
# HST and 4 IUE, measured on 2026-11-07 by comparing every BEST_ record against
# ica/manual_fix_overrides.json and finalrun/iue/iue_overrides.json.  Those 45
# were made with iterate_fit's command-line --mask flags rather than through the
# GUI, so nothing wrote them to a store and the record is the only copy.  Losing
# them would mean remasking 45 objects by hand.  The figures, the rebinned
# products and the staged exposures are all regenerable without human judgement
# and stay ignored.
!chosen_visit/
chosen_visit/*
!chosen_visit/fits/
chosen_visit/fits/*
!chosen_visit/fits/*/
chosen_visit/fits/*/*
!chosen_visit/fits/*/records/
!chosen_visit/fits/*/records/*.json
